 policy for  quite a bit of money relative to what  you are originally paid in but also  whole life insurance isn't the type that  costs a dollar a month the dollar a  month stuff is term life insurance but  the bigger picture is term life  insurance  whole life insurance neither is health  insurance which is what Donald Trump  seems to be confused about there isn't  health insurance for $1 a month in the  market the Kaiser Family Foundation  estimates that the average American  yearly premium for a sort of  middle-of-the-road individual plan  offered through the Obamacare exchanges  in 2016 was about 4500 dollars per year  or just under $400 a month this is red  alert level and competence Pat the  person who ran a presidential campaign  claiming that he would fix healthcare  for the entire country doesn't realize  the difference between term life  insurance he sees advertised on TV and  health insurance I guess you do have to  give him a pass though because Donald  Trump just recently found out that  health care is a complicated issue it  just it doesn't make too much sense to  me how could you even if you're in your  billionaire bubble think that health  care could cost someone only $12 a year  when it's the top reason for  bankruptcies in the United States when  we're having such a vigorous debate over  this and when people are going to  needlessly die if the ACA was repealed  there's just no way what occurred to me  was if you're trump and you're this  billionaire right and you've been eating  out of a silver spoon your entire life  maybe for you you don't even understand  like maybe $12 a year and 4,500 dollars  a year to Trump are basically the same  thing like for him it's like oh yeah  people are up in arms because it's a lot  of money for them and maybe the Trump  hearing that something is $12 a year  sounds like not very much and hearing  that something is $4,500 a year also  doesn't sound like very much and he just  genuinely has no idea what this stuff  